      "rev_n_1_ef57f4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_ef57f4_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_ef57f4",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the bridge operation step-by-step, keeping track of when the bridge is raised and lowered.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534527.4485958
      },
      "rev_n_2_339c4d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_339c4d_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_339c4d",
        "thought_text": "Use a priority queue to manage boats waiting to cross, prioritizing those arriving earlier.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534527.44861
      },
      "rev_n_3_186d6b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_186d6b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_186d6b",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the optimal bridge operation schedule by considering the time between boat arrivals and the bridge's raise/lower time.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534527.4486182
      },
      "rev_n_1_ef57f4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_ef57f4_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_ef57f4",
        "thought_text": "The current approach simulates the bridge operation step-by-step, but it doesn't accurately account for the time the bridge remains raised when there are boats waiting. This can lead to incorrect calculations of the total unavailable time. A more accurate approach would be to track the bridge's state (raised or lowered) and the time it remains in each state, considering the waiting time for boats and the time it takes to raise and lower the bridge.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_ef57f4_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_26b0633fbb",
        "created_at": 1794534550.1976874
      },
      "rev_n_2_339c4d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_339c4d_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_339c4d",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using a priority queue is correct, but the implementation needs to be adjusted to handle the bridge's state more accurately. Instead of just tracking the bridge's up and down times, we should also consider the state of boats waiting to cross and the time it takes for them to pass through. This will ensure that we account for the total time the bridge is unavailable, including the time it takes for boats to pass through when the bridge is raised.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_339c4d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b051b388a4",
        "created_at": 1794534581.5175664
      },
      "rev_n_3_186d6b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_186d6b_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_186d6b",
        "thought_text": "The current approach doesn't account for the possibility that the bridge can remain open longer than necessary if the next boat arrives soon after the current one. This can lead to unnecessary bridge up time. A better approach would be to consider the time between boat arrivals and optimize the bridge operation accordingly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_186d6b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ce961ac4a9",
        "created_at": 1794534606.4605713
      },
